# Code Standards

## Language

| Context | Language |
|---------|----------|
| Source code (identifiers, files, folders, commits) | **English** |
| Code comments and JSDoc | **English** |
| User-facing copy (UI, emails, disclaimers) | **Portuguese (pt-BR)** |
| Planning docs (`.cursor/plans/`) | Portuguese OK |

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
class UpdatePricesBatch { }
const isPriceStale = product.price.isStale;
// UI string: "Ver preço na Amazon"

// ❌ BAD
class AtualizarPrecosEmLote { }
const precoDesatualizado = true;
```

Domain terms in English: `Price` (not `Preco`), `PriceAlert`, `WishlistItem`. PRD Portuguese names map 1:1 to English types.

## Linting and formatting

- **ESLint** flat config with `@typescript-eslint` recommended-type-checked rules
- **Prettier** for formatting; ESLint handles logic, Prettier handles style — no conflicting rules
- Root scripts: `lint`, `lint:fix`, `format`, `format:check` via Turborepo/pnpm workspaces
- **Zero warnings** on CI for touched packages; fix or explicitly disable with comment + reason

Required ESLint posture (enable when scaffold exists):

- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`: error
- `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`: error
- `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars`: error (prefix `_` for intentionally unused)
- `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-assertions`: error (`assertionStyle: 'never'` — only `as const` allowed)
- `@typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type`: warn on exported functions in `packages/domain` and `packages/application`
- `no-console`: warn in apps (use structured logger in infrastructure)

## TypeScript typing

- **Ban** `as Type` assertions; use type guards, generics, or Zod + domain parsers instead.
- **Return types** must be explicit on exported/public APIs and use case `execute()` methods.
- **Prefer generics** over `unknown` + cast when the type relationship is known at the call site.
- **Cache/JSON boundaries:** `CacheStore.get()` returns `unknown | null`; callers validate with type guards before use.
- **Tests:** mock factories with full interface implementations — no `as never`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
async execute(slug: string): Promise<Product | null> { ... }
function parseMarketplace(value: string): Marketplace { ... }
function isPriceHistoryResult(value: unknown): value is PriceHistoryResult { ... }

// ❌ BAD
async execute(slug: string) { ... }
const data = JSON.parse(raw) as Product;
productRepository as never;
```

## Naming

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Files (domain/use cases) | PascalCase | `Product.ts`, `GetProductBySlug.ts` |
| Files (infra/adapters) | kebab-case or dot suffix | `product.repository.ts`, `amazon-fetcher.strategy.ts` |
| Classes / types / enums | PascalCase | `PriceComplianceService` |
| Functions / methods / vars | camelCase | `findDueForPriceRefresh` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_WISHLIST_ITEMS` |
| Interfaces (ports) | `I` prefix optional; prefer plain name | `ProductRepository` or `IProductRepository` — pick one, stay consistent |
| Zod schemas | `*Schema` suffix | `CreatePriceAlertSchema` |
| Test files | `*.test.ts` colocated or `__tests__/` | `Price.test.ts` |

## Modules and exports

- Prefer **named exports**; avoid default exports (easier refactor and tree-shaking)
- Path aliases: `@domain/*`, `@application/*`, `@infrastructure/*` — no deep relative imports crossing package boundaries (`../../../`)
- One public class/function per file when practical; barrel `index.ts` only at package entrypoints

## Imports order

1. Node built-ins
2. External packages
3. Monorepo packages (`@domain/...`)
4. Relative imports

Blank line between groups; use ESLint `import/order` or equivalent.

## Error handling

- Domain: throw `DomainError` subclasses with stable `code`
- Use cases: `Result<T, E>` for expected failures; throw only for programmer errors
- Adapters: map domain errors to HTTP status in one place (`errorHandler` middleware)

## Git hygiene

- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`
- Small focused PRs; no drive-by refactors
- Pre-commit (when configured): `lint-staged` → eslint --fix + prettier on staged `*.{ts,tsx,json,md}`

## Do not

- Disable ESLint/Prettier globally to pass CI
- Mix Portuguese identifiers in new code
- Commit `.env`, secrets, or generated artifacts without gitignore
- Use `// @ts-ignore` without adjacent explanation
